body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in v4.6.1.stable, v4.6.2.stable
- Not reproducible in v4.0.0.stable

### System information

Godot v4.6.1.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.3.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M3 Pro (11 threads) - 18.00 GiB memory

### Issue description

When a spatial shader includes a .gdshaderinc file and calls distance_player_to_fragment() (defined in that file), the editor hangs for ~30 seconds and spams approximately 35,000 error lines:

```
ERROR: servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shader_rd.cpp:1004 - code:
[~5000 lines of generated GLSL ommitted for brevity]
ERROR: servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shader_rd.cpp:306 - Condition "variant_stages.is_empty()" is true.
```

The above repeats several times.

If I have the _exact_ code from the included function inlined manually (renaming arguments to their corresponding variables) then the shader compiles instantly & without error. If I have an (unrelated) uniform declaration commented out, the bug seems to stop occurring, but the shader produces no outcome (the mesh totally disappears). This is likely the actual result of of the `distance_player_to_fragment()` function with the arguments set to 0, however.

I'm not actually sure what I did that triggered the bug - I was working in a different area of the game and noticed the program was suddenly hanging. 

Expected behaviour: I assume there's something deeply cursed about the `distance_player_to_fragment()` function, but I'm not sure what it could be, since it was working fine earlier. Either way, Godot should give a nice error message if there's an issue w/ the function, it shouldn't spam ~35,000 lines of error message.

This is the usage code (note that the issue also arises when real values are passed ot the function, they just aren't necessary for reproduction):

```
shader_type spatial;
#include "uid://mwi2e2lcnveh"

uniform vec3 vis_offset = vec3(0.0, 0.0, 0.0); // <-- If this line is commented out, the bug stops occurring, but the 

void fragment()
{
	float dist = distance_player_to_fragment(vec3(0,0,0), vec3(0,0,0), VIEWPORT_SIZE, PROJECTION_MATRIX, VIEW_MATRIX, vec2(0,0));
	ALPHA = dist;
}
```

and this is the .gdshaderinc file

```
float distance_player_to_fragment(vec3 player_pos_world, vec3 fragment_world, vec2 viewport_size, mat4 projection_matrix, mat4 view_matrix, vec2 vis_offset) {
	float aspect_ratio = viewport_size.x / viewport_size.y;
	vec4 clip_player = projection_matrix * view_matrix * vec4(player_pos_world, 1.0);
	vec4 clip_fragment = projection_matrix * view_matrix * vec4(fragment_world, 1.0);
	clip_player.xy /= clip_player.w;
	clip_fragment.xy /= clip_fragment.w;
	clip_player.x *= aspect_ratio;
	clip_fragment.x *= aspect_ratio;
	float dist = distance(clip_player.xy + vis_offset, clip_fragment.xy);
	return dist;
}
```

### Steps to reproduce

Issue happens for me upon opening attached MRP file.

